{"name":"Welcome White","hex":"#f3e3ca","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"welcome","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Whose arrival is a cause of joy; received with gladness; admitted willingly to the house, entertainment, or company.","Producing gladness."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Greeting given upon someone's arrival.","Ellipsis of you're welcome.."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/welcome"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Welcome","blocks":[{"text":"A welcome is a kind of greeting designed to introduce a person to a new place or situation, and to make them feel at ease. The term can similarly be used to describe the feeling of being accepted on the part of the new person."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Coir_mat1.jpg/330px-Coir_mat1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welcome","wikidata":"Q13109234"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/De